#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:238
msgid "genspider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:240
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy genspider [-t template] <name> <domain or URL>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:243
msgid ""
"Creates a new spider in the current folder or in the current project's "
"``spiders`` folder, if called from inside a project. The ``<name>`` "
"parameter is set as the spider's ``name``, while ``<domain or URL>`` is used "
"to generate the ``allowed_domains`` and ``start_urls`` spider's attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:247
msgid ""
"$ scrapy genspider -l\n"
"Available templates:\n"
"  basic\n"
"  crawl\n"
"  csvfeed\n"
"  xmlfeed\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy genspider example example.com\n"
"Created spider 'example' using template 'basic'\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy genspider -t crawl scrapyorg scrapy.org\n"
"Created spider 'scrapyorg' using template 'crawl'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:260
msgid ""
"This is just a convenient shortcut command for creating spiders based on pre-"
"defined templates, but certainly not the only way to create spiders. You can "
"just create the spider source code files yourself, instead of using this "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:268
msgid "Custom spider templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:270
msgid ""
"To define your own spider templates, point :setting:`TEMPLATES_DIR` at a "
"directory with a :file:`spiders` subdirectory, and write a :file:`{name}."
"tmpl` file there for every template, where *name* is the value to pass to ``-"
"t``. Your templates replace the built-in ones, which live in the :file:"
"`templates` directory of the ``scrapy`` package, so copy over any of those "
"that you want to keep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:277
msgid ""
"Alternatively, pass ``-t`` a path to a :file:`.tmpl` file instead of a name, "
"to use it without touching :setting:`TEMPLATES_DIR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:280
msgid ""
"Templates are rendered with :class:`string.Template`: ``$variable`` and "
"``${variable}`` are replaced, and ``$$`` renders as a single ``$``, which "
"regular expressions often need. Rendering fails on any variable other than "
"the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:285
msgid "``name``: the spider name, as passed to the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:287
msgid ""
"``module``: *name* as a valid module name, also used as the file name of the "
"generated spider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:290
msgid "``classname``: *module* in camel case, with a ``Spider`` suffix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:292
msgid ""
"``url``: the URL passed to the command, with an ``https`` scheme added if it "
"had none."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:295
msgid "``domain``: the domain of *url*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:297
msgid "``project_name``: :setting:`BOT_NAME`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:299
msgid "``ProjectName``: *project_name* in camel case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:304
msgid "crawl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:306
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy crawl <spider>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:307 ../../../topics/commands.rst:340
#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:385 ../../../topics/commands.rst:402
#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:533
msgid "Requires project: *yes*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:309
msgid ""
"Start crawling using the spider with the given :attr:`~scrapy.Spider.name`, "
"which must be one of those that :command:`list` reports. To run a spider "
"from a file instead, use :command:`runspider`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:313 ../../../topics/commands.rst:435
#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:475 ../../../topics/commands.rst:499
#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:538
msgid "Supported options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:315
msgid "``-h, --help``: show a help message and exit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:317
msgid "``-a NAME=VALUE``: set a spider argument (may be repeated)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:319
msgid ""
"``--output FILE`` or ``-o FILE``: append scraped items to the end of FILE "
"(use - for stdout). To define the output format, set a colon at the end of "
"the output URI (i.e. ``-o FILE:FORMAT``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:321
msgid ""
"``--overwrite-output FILE`` or ``-O FILE``: dump scraped items into FILE, "
"overwriting any existing file. To define the output format, set a colon at "
"the end of the output URI (i.e. ``-O FILE:FORMAT``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:323 ../../../topics/commands.rst:346
#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:443
msgid "Usage examples::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:325
msgid ""
"$ scrapy crawl myspider\n"
"[ ... myspider starts crawling ... ]\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy crawl -o myfile:csv myspider\n"
"[ ... myspider starts crawling and appends the result to the file myfile in "
"csv format ... ]\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy crawl -O myfile:json myspider\n"
"[ ... myspider starts crawling and saves the result in myfile in json format "
"overwriting the original content... ]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:337
msgid "check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:339
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy check [-l] <spider>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:342
msgid "Run contract checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:348
msgid ""
"$ scrapy check -l\n"
"first_spider\n"
"  * parse\n"
"  * parse_item\n"
"second_spider\n"
"  * parse\n"
"  * parse_item\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy check\n"
"F.F.\n"
"======================================================================\n"
"FAIL: [first_spider] parse (@returns post-hook)\n"
"----------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  ...\n"
"scrapy.exceptions.ContractFail: Returned 92 requests, expected 0..4\n"
"\n"
"======================================================================\n"
"FAIL: [first_spider] parse_item (@scrapes post-hook)\n"
"----------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"  ...\n"
"scrapy.exceptions.ContractFail: Missing fields: RetailPricex\n"
"\n"
"----------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"Ran 4 contracts in 0.174s\n"
"\n"
"FAILED (failures=2)"
msgstr ""

