#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:418
msgid "fetch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:420
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy fetch <url>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:423
msgid ""
"Downloads the given URL using the Scrapy downloader and writes the contents "
"to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:426
msgid ""
"The interesting thing about this command is that it fetches the page the way "
"the spider would download it. For example, if the spider has a "
"``USER_AGENT`` attribute which overrides the User Agent, it will use that "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:430
msgid ""
"So this command can be used to \"see\" how your spider would fetch a certain "
"page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:432
msgid ""
"If used outside a project, no particular per-spider behaviour would be "
"applied and it will just use the default Scrapy downloader settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:437 ../../../topics/commands.rst:477
#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:501 ../../../topics/commands.rst:540
msgid ""
"``--spider=SPIDER``: bypass spider autodetection and force use of specific "
"spider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:439
msgid ""
"``--headers``: print the request's and response's HTTP headers instead of "
"the response's body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:441 ../../../topics/commands.rst:479
msgid ""
"``--no-redirect``: do not follow HTTP 3xx redirects (default is to follow "
"them)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:445
msgid ""
"$ scrapy fetch --nolog http://www.example.com/some/page.html\n"
"[ ... html content here ... ]\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy fetch --nolog --headers http://www.example.com/\n"
"> Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8\n"
"> Accept-Language: en\n"
"> User-Agent: Scrapy/2.16.0 (+https://scrapy.org)\n"
"> Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br, zstd\n"
">\n"
"< Date: Wed, 08 Jul 2026 06:15:01 GMT\n"
"< Content-Type: text/html\n"
"< Server: cloudflare\n"
"< Last-Modified: Wed, 01 Jul 2026 17:50:18 GMT\n"
"< Allow: GET, HEAD\n"
"< Cf-Cache-Status: HIT\n"
"< Age: 8184\n"
"< Cf-Ray: a17cf3b80eddf141-DME"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:466
msgid "view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:468
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy view <url>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:471
msgid ""
"Opens the given URL in a browser, as your Scrapy spider would \"see\" it. "
"Sometimes spiders see pages differently from regular users, so this can be "
"used to check what the spider \"sees\" and confirm it's what you expect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:483
msgid ""
"$ scrapy view http://www.example.com/some/page.html\n"
"[ ... browser starts ... ]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:489
msgid "shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:491
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy shell [url]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:494
msgid ""
"Starts the Scrapy shell for the given URL (if given) or empty if no URL is "
"given. Also supports UNIX-style local file paths, either relative with ``./"
"`` or ``../`` prefixes or absolute file paths. See :ref:`topics-shell` for "
"more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:503
msgid "``-c code``: evaluate the code in the shell, print the result and exit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:505
msgid ""
"``--no-redirect``: do not follow HTTP 3xx redirects (default is to follow "
"them); this only affects the URL you may pass as argument on the command "
"line; once you are inside the shell, ``fetch(url)`` will still follow HTTP "
"redirects by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:511
msgid ""
"$ scrapy shell http://www.example.com/some/page.html\n"
"[ ... scrapy shell starts ... ]\n"
"\n"
"$ scrapy shell --nolog http://www.example.com/ -c '(response.status, "
"response.url)'\n"
"(200, 'http://www.example.com/')\n"
"\n"
"# shell follows HTTP redirects by default\n"
"$ scrapy shell --nolog http://httpbin.org/redirect-to?"
"url=http%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F -c '(response.status, response.url)'\n"
"(200, 'http://example.com/')\n"
"\n"
"# you can disable this with --no-redirect\n"
"# (only for the URL passed as command line argument)\n"
"$ scrapy shell --no-redirect --nolog http://httpbin.org/redirect-to?"
"url=http%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F -c '(response.status, response.url)'\n"
"(302, 'http://httpbin.org/redirect-to?url=http%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:530
msgid "parse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:532
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy parse <url> [options]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:535
msgid ""
"Fetches the given URL and parses it with the spider that handles it, using "
"the method passed with the ``--callback`` option, or ``parse`` if not given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:542
msgid "``-a NAME=VALUE``: set spider argument (may be repeated)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:544
msgid ""
"``--callback`` or ``-c``: spider method to use as callback for parsing the "
"response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:547
msgid ""
"``--meta`` or ``-m``: additional request meta that will be passed to the "
"callback request. This must be a valid json string. Example: --"
"meta='{\"foo\" : \"bar\"}'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:550
msgid ""
"``--cbkwargs``: additional keyword arguments that will be passed to the "
"callback. This must be a valid json string. Example: --cbkwargs='{\"foo\" : "
"\"bar\"}'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:553
msgid ""
"``--pipelines``: :ref:`process items through pipelines <test-item-pipeline>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:555
msgid ""
"``--rules`` or ``-r``: use :class:`~scrapy.spiders.CrawlSpider` rules to "
"discover the callback (i.e. spider method) to use for parsing the response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:559
msgid "``--noitems``: don't show scraped items"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:561
msgid "``--nolinks``: don't show extracted links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:563
msgid "``--nocolour``: avoid using pygments to colorize the output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:565
msgid ""
"``--depth`` or ``-d``: depth level for which the requests should be followed "
"recursively (default: 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:568
msgid "``--verbose`` or ``-v``: display information for each depth level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:570
msgid "``--output`` or ``-o``: dump scraped items to a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:576
msgid ""
"$ scrapy parse http://www.example.com/ -c parse_item\n"
"[ ... scrapy log lines crawling example.com spider ... ]\n"
"\n"
">>> STATUS DEPTH LEVEL 1 <<<\n"
"# Scraped Items  "
"------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"[{'name': 'Example item',\n"
" 'category': 'Furniture',\n"
" 'length': '12 cm'}]\n"
"\n"
"# Requests  "
"-----------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"[]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:594
msgid "settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:596
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy settings [options]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:599
msgid "Get the value of a Scrapy setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:601
msgid ""
"If used inside a project it'll show the project setting value, otherwise "
"it'll show the default Scrapy value for that setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:604 ../../../topics/commands.rst:623
msgid "Example usage::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:606
msgid ""
"$ scrapy settings --get BOT_NAME\n"
"scrapybot\n"
"$ scrapy settings --get DOWNLOAD_DELAY\n"
"0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:614
msgid "runspider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:616
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy runspider <spider_file.py>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:619
msgid ""
"Run the spider defined in the given Python file, without requiring a project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:621
msgid "Supported options: the same as :command:`crawl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:625
msgid ""
"$ scrapy runspider myspider.py\n"
"[ ... spider starts crawling ... ]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:631
msgid "version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:633
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy version [-v]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:636
msgid ""
"Prints the Scrapy version. If used with ``-v`` it also prints Python, "
"Twisted and Platform info, which is useful for bug reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:642
msgid "bench"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:644
msgid "Syntax: ``scrapy bench``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:647
msgid "Run a quick benchmark test. :ref:`benchmarking`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:652
msgid "Commands that run a crawl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:654
msgid ""
"Many commands need to run a crawl of some kind, running either a user-"
"provided spider or a special internal one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:666
msgid ""
"They use an internal instance of :class:`scrapy.crawler.AsyncCrawlerProcess` "
"or :class:`scrapy.crawler.CrawlerProcess` for this. In most cases this "
"detail shouldn't matter to the user running the command, but when the user :"
"ref:`needs a non-default Twisted reactor <disable-asyncio>`, it may be "
"important."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:671
msgid ""
"Scrapy decides which of these two classes to use based on the value of the :"
"setting:`TWISTED_REACTOR` and :setting:`TWISTED_REACTOR_ENABLED` settings. "
"With :setting:`TWISTED_REACTOR_ENABLED` set to ``False`` it will use :class:"
"`~scrapy.crawler.AsyncCrawlerProcess`. Otherwise, if the :setting:"
"`TWISTED_REACTOR` value is the default one (``'twisted.internet."
"asyncioreactor.AsyncioSelectorReactor'``), :class:`~scrapy.crawler."
"AsyncCrawlerProcess` will be used, otherwise :class:`~scrapy.crawler."
"CrawlerProcess` will be used. The :ref:`spider settings <spider-settings>` "
"are not taken into account when doing this, as they are loaded after this "
"decision is made. This may cause an error if the project-level setting is "
"set to :ref:`the asyncio reactor <install-asyncio>` (:ref:`explicitly "
"<project-settings>` or :ref:`by using the Scrapy default <default-"
"settings>`) and :ref:`the setting of the spider being run <spider-settings>` "
"is set to :ref:`a different one <disable-asyncio>`, because :class:`~scrapy."
"crawler.AsyncCrawlerProcess` only supports the asyncio reactor. In this case "
"you should set the :setting:`FORCE_CRAWLER_PROCESS` setting to ``True`` (at "
"the project level or via the command line) so that Scrapy uses :class:"
"`~scrapy.crawler.CrawlerProcess` which supports all reactors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:691
msgid "Custom project commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:693
msgid ""
"You can also add your custom project commands by using the :setting:"
"`COMMANDS_MODULE` setting. This allows you to create project-specific "
"commands that are automatically discovered and made available through the "
"``scrapy`` command-line tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:699
msgid "Creating custom commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:701
msgid ""
"To create a custom command, inherit from the :class:`~scrapy.commands."
"ScrapyCommand` class and implement the required methods. This allows you to "
"extend Scrapy's command-line interface with your own functionality, such as "
"project-specific utilities, data processing tools, or deployment helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:706
msgid ""
"When you create a custom command, you define its behavior by setting class "
"attributes and overriding specific methods. Here's what you need to know:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:709
msgid "**Attributes you can set:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:711
msgid ""
":attr:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.requires_project` (bool): If ``True``, "
"the command only runs inside a Scrapy project (default: ``False``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:713
msgid ""
":attr:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.requires_crawler_process` (bool): If "
"``True``, a :class:`~scrapy.crawler.AsyncCrawlerProcess` or :class:`~scrapy."
"crawler.CrawlerProcess` instance will be created by Scrapy when the command "
"runs and made available in the :attr:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand."
"crawler_process` attribute (default: ``True``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:719
msgid ""
":attr:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.default_settings` (dict): Settings "
"that will override the default ones when running this command (default: ``{}"
"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:721
msgid ""
":attr:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.exitcode` (int): Process exit code to "
"set when the command completes (default: ``0``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:724
msgid "**Methods you must override:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:726
msgid ""
":meth:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.short_desc`: Return a short "
"description of the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:728
msgid ""
":meth:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.run`: Main entry point for the command "
"execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:731
msgid "**Methods you can override:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:733
msgid ""
":meth:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.syntax`: Return command syntax "
"(preferably one-line, without command name)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:735
msgid ""
":meth:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.long_desc`: Return a detailed command "
"description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:737
msgid ""
":meth:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.add_options`: Add command-specific "
"options to the argument parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:739
msgid ""
":meth:`~scrapy.commands.ScrapyCommand.process_options`: Process parsed "
"command-line options and set settings before :attr:`~scrapy.commands."
"ScrapyCommand.crawler_process` is instantiated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:743
msgid "**Example custom command:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:745
msgid ""
"from scrapy.commands import ScrapyCommand\n"
"import argparse\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class MyCustomCommand(ScrapyCommand):\n"
"    requires_project = True\n"
"\n"
"    def syntax(self):\n"
"        return \"[options] <spider_name>\"\n"
"\n"
"    def short_desc(self):\n"
"        return \"Run my custom command\"\n"
"\n"
"    def add_options(self, parser):\n"
"        super().add_options(parser)\n"
"        parser.add_argument(\"--my-option\", help=\"My custom option\")\n"
"\n"
"    def run(self, args, opts):\n"
"        # Command implementation here\n"
"        spider_name = args[0] if args else None\n"
"        print(f\"Running custom command for spider: {spider_name}\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:769
msgid ""
"For real examples, see the built-in Scrapy commands in the `scrapy/"
"commands`_ directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:777
msgid "This is a :ref:`pre-crawler setting <pre-crawler-settings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:782
msgid "Register commands via setup.py entry points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:784
msgid ""
"You can also add Scrapy commands from an external library by adding a "
"``scrapy.commands`` section in the entry points of the library ``setup.py`` "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:788
msgid "The following example adds ``my_command`` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:792
msgid ""
"from setuptools import setup, find_packages\n"
"\n"
"setup(\n"
"    name=\"scrapy-mymodule\",\n"
"    entry_points={\n"
"        \"scrapy.commands\": [\n"
"            \"my_command=my_scrapy_module.commands:MyCommand\",\n"
"        ],\n"
"    },\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:808
msgid "COMMANDS_MODULE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:810
msgid "Default: ``''`` (empty string)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:812
msgid ""
"A module to use for looking up custom Scrapy commands. This is used to add "
"custom commands for your Scrapy project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:815
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/commands.rst:817
msgid "COMMANDS_MODULE = \"mybot.commands\""
msgstr ""
